# The website is the repository root, served as static files (vercel.json): index.html,
# sw.js, manifest.json, privacy.html, the icons, fonts/, avatars/, .well-known/ and the
# build stamp (scripts/vercel-build-info.js writes buildInfo.js). Everything else is left
# out, so each deployment is small (Vercel's free plan has 10 GB for all of them) and
# nothing internal is served at ledger.sgj.luxe.

# the iOS and Android projects: built on a Mac, never served
native/

# tests, the Cloud Functions and Firebase's config: deployed to Firebase by hand
tests/
functions/
firebase.json
.firebaserc
firestore.rules
firestore.indexes.json

# documents and coordination notes
docs/
CLAUDE.md
PROJECT_LEDGER.md
.github/

# GitHub Pages only (the legacy site)
_config.yml
buildInfo.pages.js

# a one-off setup script; the build step it sits beside is kept
scripts/setup-github-deploy.sh
